<%# The locality-emergence sweep's pre-registered reading (docs/design_record.md, 2026-09-27):
    `reading` is a Lab::LocalityEmergenceReading::Report. The per-run rows stay in
    `lab:locality_emergence_report`. %>
<% peak = reading.peak %>
<% shape = reading.shape %>
<section class="mt-6" id="locality-emergence-reading">
  <h2>
    The pre-registered reading
    <span class="badge <%= reading.interim? ? 'badge-warning' : 'badge-success' %>">
      <%= reading.interim? ? "interim" : "final" %>
    </span>
  </h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted">
    <% if reading.interim? %>
      Interim: not every run of the sweep has finished, and only the finished ones are counted.
      Nothing here is the sweep's result yet.
    <% else %>
      Every run of the sweep has finished.
    <% end %>
    A run emerged where it has a confirmed emergence epoch and reads
    <span class="mono">replicator_share</span> of at least
    <%= percent_value Lab::LocalityEmergenceReading::MIN_SHARE %> at some sample from it on,
    as in the lineage-diversity sweep.
  </p>

  <figure class="table-figure mt-4">
    <figcaption class="table-caption text-sm text-muted" id="locality-emergence-arms">
      Runs per arm, counted so far. The rate is emerged over finished.
    </figcaption>
    <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="locality-emergence-arms">
      <table class="data-table" aria-labelledby="locality-emergence-arms">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Arm</th>
            <th class="numeric">Runs</th>
            <th class="numeric">Finished</th>
            <th class="numeric">Emerged</th>
            <th class="numeric">Rate</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% reading.arms.each do |arm| %>
            <tr>
              <td><%= arm.label %></td>
              <td class="numeric"><%= arm.rows.size %></td>
              <td class="numeric"><%= arm.finished %></td>
              <td class="numeric"><%= arm.emerged %></td>
              <td class="numeric"><%= percent_value arm.rate&.to_f %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </figure>

  <h3 class="mt-4">H-peak</h3>
  <p>
    Radius <%= Lab::LocalityEmergenceReading::PEAK_RADIUS %> emerges more often than radius 1 and than
    the well-mixed world:
    <span class="badge <%= peak.badge_class %>"><%= peak.outcome_label %></span>
  </p>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted">
    <% if peak.testable? %>
      Two one-sided Fisher exact tests, Holm-corrected at family level
      <%= Lab::LocalityEmergenceReading::FAMILY_ALPHA %>:
      <%= peak.comparisons.join("; ") %>.
    <% else %>
      Untested until radius <%= Lab::LocalityEmergenceReading::PEAK_RADIUS %>, radius 1 and the
      well-mixed arm each have a finished run.
    <% end %>
  </p>

  <h3 class="mt-4">H-shape</h3>
  <p>
    Across the finite radii, emergence peaks at an intermediate reach:
    <span class="badge <%= shape.badge_class %>"><%= shape.outcome_label %></span>
  </p>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted">
    A logistic regression of emergence on radius and radius² over the finished runs of radius
    <%= Lab::LocalityEmergenceReading::SHAPE_RADII.to_sentence %>, read where the radius²
    coefficient is negative at two-sided Wald p &lt; <%= Lab::LocalityEmergenceReading::SHAPE_LEVEL %>
    and the fitted peak lies between radius <%= Lab::LocalityEmergenceReading::SHAPE_RADII.min %> and
    <%= Lab::LocalityEmergenceReading::SHAPE_RADII.max %>.
    <% if shape.fit %>
      The radius² coefficient is <%= metric_value shape.fit.quadratic %>, Wald
      p = <%= metric_value shape.fit.wald_p %>, and the fitted peak
      <%= shape.peak ? "is at radius #{metric_value shape.peak}" : "does not exist: the curve opens upward" %>.
    <% elsif shape.testable? %>
      The fit did not settle.
    <% else %>
      Untested until <%= Lab::LocalityEmergenceReading::MIN_SHAPE_RADII %> finite radii have a
      finished run, with emerged and not-emerged runs among them.
    <% end %>
    <% if shape.well_mixed_arm&.finished? %>
      Well-mixed is not a distance and is left out of the fit: it emerged
      <%= shape.well_mixed_arm.emerged %> of <%= shape.well_mixed_arm.finished %>.
    <% end %>
  </p>
</section>
